    <name>
      <text>Inverse of Polynomials — inverse of a linear function</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let \( f(x) = {@m@}x + {@b@} \).</p>
<p>Find \( f^{-1}(x) \).</p>
<div>\( f^{-1}(x) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>To find the inverse: write \(y={@m@}x+{@b@}\), swap \(x\) and \(y\) to get \(x={@m@}y+{@b@}\), then solve for \(y\):</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
x &= {@m@}y+{@b@}\\
x-{@b@} &= {@m@}y\\
y &= \dfrac{x-{@b@}}{ {@m@} }
\end{align*}
\]
<p>So \(f^{-1}(x)=\dfrac{x-{@b@}}{ {@m@} }\). A common mistake is dividing \(x\) by \({@m@}\) but forgetting to also divide \({@b@}\) by \({@m@}\), or getting the sign of \({@b@}\) wrong when moving it across.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
